    "summary_insights": [
      "Revenue grew by 8.6% year-on-year, reaching £1.78m, driven primarily by core sales.",
      "Gross margin compressed from 47.4% to 44.0% due to a 15.7% increase in cost of sales, particularly direct labour and subcontractor costs.",
      "Operating profit more than doubled (+124.6%) to £253.9k, largely due to a significant reduction in administrative expenses.",
      "Administrative expenses fell by 20.4%, primarily driven by a sharp reduction in directors' salaries from £116k to £9.5k.",
      "Net profit margin improved significantly from 5.4% to 10.9%, reflecting much stronger bottom-line efficiency.",
      "The company eliminated interest-bearing debt costs in 2025, improving financial resilience.",
      "Staff costs (excluding directors) rose by 16.6%, indicating increased operational scale or wage inflation.",
      "Overall profitability has strengthened considerably, though the decline in gross margin warrants monitoring of direct cost controls."
    ]
