    "summary_insights": [
      "Net assets grew significantly by 53.3%, rising from £362,845 to £556,156, driven by strong retained profitability.",
      "The current ratio improved from 2.02 to 2.94, indicating a robust and strengthening short-term liquidity position.",
      "Tangible fixed assets increased by 59.8%, primarily due to significant investment in motor vehicles, which rose from £86,273 to £148,648.",
      "Intercompany receivables (amounts owed by group undertakings) surged from £6,487 to £212,457, representing a substantial shift in asset allocation.",
      "The quick ratio remains healthy at 1.88, though it slightly decreased from 1.93 as more liquidity is tied up in intercompany debts rather than cash.",
      "Long-term liabilities increased due to new hire purchase obligations of £57,200, resulting in the gearing ratio rising from 7.0% to 17.6%.",
      "Cash at bank decreased by 33.7% (£362,769 to £240,408), likely due to the combined impact of fixed asset acquisitions and increased intercompany lending.",
      "A new related party liability of £27,852 is owed to directors at year-end 2025, which was not present in the prior year."
